--- !u!114 &1579766862644791944
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2ad88bbb0ce7b86478477c5086507618, type: 3}
  m_Name: Maren_WindKeeper_Knowledge
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  knownFacts:
  - topic: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8e73c156320583c48a35d9baa9267ff4, type: 2}
    text: There is a steady current between the two big islands. A small boat is
      fastest at dawn.
    oneTime: 0
    reveal: 0
    threshold: 0
    flagKey: 
  - topic: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9d74f7aa73eac464993f55e6d2eaf9a7, type: 2}
    text: Jorin lives south. He fixes anything that turns or blows.
    oneTime: 0
    reveal: 0
    threshold: 0
    flagKey: 
  - topic: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 83328c98f159646408b0ad7c9a4a8461, type: 2}
    text: The shrine has stood since before my grandmother's grandmother. Its bells
      are bronze, off a wrecked trading ship. They ring when the air moves right.
    oneTime: 0
    reveal: 0
    threshold: 0
    flagKey: 
  - topic: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 69f4e34e31b0a684594cf7699a570d92, type: 2}
    text: "The gulls nest on the south cliff. They go quiet about half a day before
      bad weather \u2014 I trust them more than any forecast."
    oneTime: 0
    reveal: 0
    threshold: 0
    flagKey: 
  - topic: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3f0738f9e433ae74caf2b665f77be587, type: 2}
    text: Twelve of us live on this island year-round. Mostly we keep to our own
      roofs. We wave when passing. That is enough.
    oneTime: 0
    reveal: 0
    threshold: 0
    flagKey: 
  - topic: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0ab236d3d62d4c441b48b78ffe879591, type: 2}
    text: A trader's ship has been circling further out for the past week. It has
      not docked. I do not like that.
    oneTime: 0
    reveal: 0
    threshold: 0
    flagKey: 
  beliefs:
  - topic: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b1c4466993707c34aaf3f4db120ab6ff, type: 2}
    text: The sky split the year I was born. Half the village still says so. I think
      it was only a bad storm.
    oneTime: 0
    reveal: 0
    threshold: 0
    flagKey: 
  - topic: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 69f4e34e31b0a684594cf7699a570d92, type: 2}
    text: Gulls remember kindness. Throw them a fish once and they will know your
      face for a season.
    oneTime: 0
    reveal: 0
    threshold: 0
    flagKey: 
  - topic: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9d74f7aa73eac464993f55e6d2eaf9a7, type: 2}
    text: Jorin has good hands but does not sleep enough. He will burn himself out
      before he is fifty if nobody tells him.
    oneTime: 0
    reveal: 0
    threshold: 0
    flagKey: 
  rumors:
  - topic: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 1e64cfd57762657459a1121080db3287, type: 2}
    text: Travelers whisper that the north cave is sealed by a song. Or by a tool.
      I forget which.
    oneTime: 0
    reveal: 1
    threshold: 40
    flagKey: 
  - topic: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 140e8e55d5d02c8469f74c9a71d24c78, type: 2}
    text: "I came here forty years ago. My husband did not come with me \u2014 the
      sea kept him. I do not speak of it often. The shrine is enough."
    oneTime: 0
    reveal: 1
    threshold: 50
    flagKey: 
  secrets:
  - topic: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 1e64cfd57762657459a1121080db3287, type: 2}
    text: The cave opens for whoever stands at the mouth when the sky tunnel blows
      north. Jorin's pumps can hold the door for one breath.
    oneTime: 0
    reveal: 1
    threshold: 75
    flagKey: 
  avoidedTopics:
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: b1c4466993707c34aaf3f4db120ab6ff, type: 2}
